1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,720
THE FAMOUS SPEECH OF PATRICK HENRY TO THE VIRGINIA HOUSE OF BURGESSES

2
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:38,620
GIVEN ON MARCH 23, 1775 AND ENTITLED GIVE ME LIBERTY OR GIVE ME DEATH.

3
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:44,600
No man thinks more highly than I do of the patriotism, as well as abilities, of the very

4
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:50,340
worthy gentlemen who have just addressed the House. But different men often see the same

5
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:56,240
subject in different lights, and therefore I hope it will not be thought disrespectful

6
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:59,840
to those gentlemen if, entertaining as I do,

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,400
opinions of a character very opposite to theirs,

8
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,800
I shall speak forth my sentiments freely and without reserve.

9
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:11,500
This is no time for ceremony.

10
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:17,200
The question before the House is one of awful moment to this country.

11
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:23,400
For my own part, I consider it as nothing less than a question of freedom or slavery,

12
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:29,500
and in proportion to the magnitude of the subject, ought to be the freedom of the debate.

13
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:33,600
It is only in this way that we can hope to arrive at truth

14
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:39,800
and fulfill the great responsibility which we hold to God and our country.

15
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:45,300
Should I keep back my opinions at such a time through fear of giving offense,

16
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:49,600
I should consider myself as guilty of treason toward my country

17
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:53,500
and of an act of disloyalty towards the Majesty of Heaven,

18
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:57,100
which I revere above all earthly kings.

19
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,100
Mr. President, it is

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,240
natural to man to indulge in the illusions of hope. We are apt to shut our

21
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:11,120
eyes against a painful truth and listen to the song of that siren till she

22
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:18,200
transforms us into beasts. Is this the part of wise men engaged in a great and

23
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:23,560
arduous struggle for liberty? Are we disposed to be of the number of those

24
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:31,080
who, having eyes, see not, and having ears, hear not the things which so nearly

25
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:37,720
concern their temporal salvation? For my part, whatever anguish of spirit it may

26
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:43,400
cost, I am willing to know the whole truth, to know the worst, and to provide

27
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:50,800
for it. I have but one lamp by which my feet are guided, and that is the lamp of

28
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:56,760
experience. I know of no way of judging of the future but by the past, and

29
00:02:56,760 --> 00:03:01,920
judging by the past I wish to know

30
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,400
what there has been in the conduct of the British ministry for the last ten

31
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:09,840
years to justify those hopes with which gentlemen have been pleased to solace

32
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:16,160
themselves and the house. Is it that insidious smile with which our petition

33
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:22,480
has been lately received? Trust it not, sir, it will prove a snare to your feet.

34
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:28,880
Suffer not yourselves to be betrayed with a kiss. Ask yourselves how this

35
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:34,520
gracious reception of our petition comports with those warlike preparations

36
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:40,360
which cover our waters and darken our land. Are fleets and armies necessary to

37
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:46,840
a work of love and reconciliation? Have we shown ourselves so unwilling to be

38
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:52,640
reconciled that force must be called in to win back our love? Let us not deceive

39
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:58,640
ourselves, sir. These are the implements of war and subjugation, the last

40
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:01,880
arguments to which

41
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:07,360
King's Resort. I ask gentlemen, sir, what means this martial array if its purpose

42
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:13,160
be not to force us to submission? Can gentlemen assign any other possible

43
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:18,840
motive for it? Has Great Britain any enemy in this quarter of the world to

44
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:26,480
call for all this accumulation of navies and armies? No, sir, she has none. They are

45
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:32,800
meant for us. They can be meant for no other. They are sent over to bind and

46
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:37,800
rivet upon us those chains which the British ministry have been so long

47
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:46,360
forging. And what have we to oppose to them? Shall we try argument? Sir, we have

48
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:53,200
been trying that for the last ten years. Have we anything new to offer upon this

49
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:59,400
subject? Nothing. We have held the subject up in every light of which it is capable,

50
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,400
but it

51
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,280
it has all been in vain.

52
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:06,100
Shall we resort to entreaty and humble supplication?

53
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:10,800
What terms shall we find which have not already been exhausted?

54
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:15,520
Let us not, I beseech you, sir, deceive ourselves.

55
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,480
Sir, we have done everything that

56
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:21,640
could be done to avert the storm which is now coming on.

57
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:23,400
We have petitioned.

58
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,120
We have remonstrated.

59
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,880
We have supplicated.

60
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:30,200
We have prostrated ourselves before the throne

61
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,240
and have implored its interposition

62
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:37,040
to arrest the tyrannical hands of the ministry and parliament.

63
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:39,880
Our petitions have been slighted.

64
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:44,880
Our remonstrances have produced additional violence and insult.

65
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:48,120
Our supplications have been disregarded.

66
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,800
And we have been spurned with contempt

67
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:53,300
from the foot of the throne.

68
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,220
In vain, after these things, may we

69
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:59,660
indulge the fond hope of peace and reconciliation.

70
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,980
there is no longer any room for hope.

71
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:07,100
If we wish to be free, if we mean

72
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:11,340
to preserve inviolate those inestimable privileges for which

73
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:15,660
we have so long been contending, if we mean not basely

74
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:18,980
to abandon the noble struggle in which we have so long been

75
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:22,540
engaged and which we have pledged ourselves never

76
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:25,740
to abandon until the glorious object of our contest

77
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:29,820
shall be obtained, we must fight.

78
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:33,500
I repeat it, sir, we must fight.

79
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,900
An appeal to arms and to the God of hosts

80
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:38,940
is all that has left us.

81
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:42,580
They tell us, sir, that we are weak,

82
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:46,500
unable to cope with so formidable an adversary.

83
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:49,180
But when shall we be stronger?

84
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:53,220
Will it be the next week or the next year?

85
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:55,900
Will it be when we are totally disarmed

86
00:06:55,900 --> 00:07:00,380
and when a British guard shall be stationed in every house?

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Shall we gather strength by irresolution and inaction?

88
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Shall we acquire the means of effectual resistance

89
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:14,000
by lying supinely on our backs and hugging the delusive phantom of hope

90
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:18,000
until our enemies shall have us bound hand and foot?

91
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Sir, we are not weak if we make a proper use of those means

92
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,000
which the God of nature hath placed in our power.

93
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:31,000
The millions of people armed in the holy cause of liberty

94
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
and in such a country as that which we possess

95
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:39,000
are invincible by any force which our enemy can send against us.

96
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Besides, sir, we shall not fight our battles alone.

97
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:49,000
There is a just God who presides over the destinies of nations

98
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
and who will raise up friends to fight our battles for us.

99
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:58,000
The battle, sir, is not to the strong alone.

100
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
It is to the vigilant.

101
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:09,440
the active and the brave. Besides, sir, we have no election. If we were base enough to desire it,

102
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:17,120
it is now too late to retire from the contest. There is no retreat but in submission and slavery.

103
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:23,520
Our chains are forged. Their clanking may be heard on the plains of Boston.

104
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:34,000
The war is inevitable and let it come. I repeat it, sir, let it come. It is in vain,

105
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:41,920
sir, to extenuate the matter. Gentlemen may cry, peace, peace, but there is no peace.

106
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:49,040
The war is actually begun. The next gale that sweeps from the north will bring to our ears

107
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:57,680
the clash of resounding arms. Our brethren are already in the field. Why stand we here idle?

108
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,760
What is it that

109
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:09,520
wish, what would they have? Is life so dear, or peace so sweet, as to be

110
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:17,000
purchased at the price of chains and slavery? Forbid it, Almighty God! I know

111
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:27,000
not what course others may take, but as for me, give me liberty, or give me death!

112
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,060
you

